WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:56.010
<b>Straight Ahead!</b>

3
00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.370
Whoa, look at that...!

4
00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:00.300
His tears are making a rainbow!

5
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.650
With all this crying,
we'll drown here.

6
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.360
It's practically a waterfall.

7
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.520
So sad... Master... Brogy!

8
00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.090
Dorry... you're... alive!

9
00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.300
I must have
lost consciousness...

10
00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.300
Mr. 0...

11
00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.810
I've heard that name
somewhere before...

12
00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.140
Wasn't that the
name of the boss guy

13
00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.940
that Vivi was so frightened of?

14
00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.830
Which would mean...

15
00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.290
...that the person
who is on the other end

16
00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.990
of this transponder snail...

17
00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.450
...is one of the
Seven Warlords of the Sea.

18
00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.300
It's been a long time since
I issued your orders, Mr. 3...

19
00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.470
What's happening on that island?

20
00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:09.280
All right,
so I guess this Mr. 3 character

21
00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.350
is the owner of this
transponder snail.

22
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.070
I think I have
this figured out now.

23
00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.010
This little place here
is an enemy hideout,

24
00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.880
and someone named Mr. 3
was ordered by someone

25
00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.080
named Mr. 0 to come to
this island and kill Vivi.

26
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.070
Damn it...
What was I thinking...?

27
00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.240
This was no time for me to
be out on a hunting trip...!

28
00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.260
I hope that
they're all still okay.

29
00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.230
Shit...

30
00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.630
Well, are you
going to answer me?

31
00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.980
When I ask a question,
I expect an answer...

32
00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.800
Have you eliminated Princess
Vivi and the Straw Hats

33
00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.150
as you were ordered?

34
00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.950
Oh, yeah, the mission
was successful.

35
00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.610
I eliminated all those
pesky brats like you said to.

36
00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:47.450
Your secret is
completely protected,

37
00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.350
so there's no need to keep
going after them anymore.

38
00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.460
I see... so...

39
00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.030
As we speak, the Unluckies
are headed your way

40
00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.900
in order to confirm the
success of your mission

41
00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.290
and to deliver
a certain package.

42
00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.060
The Unluckies. Of course...

43
00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.300
And a package?

44
00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:08.210
It's an eternal pose that will
point you to Alabasta Kingdom.

45
00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:09.190
Once that arrives,

46
00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.110
you and Miss Golden Week
will head for Alabasta.

47
00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:15.470
It's time for the
next phase of the plan.

48
00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.520
We are about to
begin embarking upon

49
00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.640
our most important
operation to date...

50
00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.240
Details will follow
after you reach Alabasta.

51
00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.750
Wait for my orders.

52
00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.980
Huh?

53
00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.180
What the...
What are those...

54
00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:34.070
Mr. 3...! What was that?!

55
00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:37.110
Oh, uh...
It's nothing... really.

56
00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.130
What the hell is that?

57
00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.600
Hmm?

58
00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.410
So I guess you're trying
to kill me, huh...?

59
00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.280
Well, monkey, bring it on.

60
00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.820
All right, you... What now...?

61
00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:16.130
So what are you gonna do now,
you oversized chicken?!

62
00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:21.780
Hey...

63
00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:22.980
What's going on...?

64
00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.630
Answer me, Mr. 3...

65
00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.300
Hey...! Well... nothing...

66
00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.780
It's just...

67
00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.480
...that damn Straw Hat
was still alive.

68
00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:34.140
It's okay, though.
I finished him off real good.

69
00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.630
No need to worry.

70
00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.730
What do you mean
he was still alive...?

71
00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:41.930
I believe that just a moment ago

72
00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:45.400
you said that your mission
was completed successfully...

73
00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.300
Isn't that correct?

74
00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.640
Yes, that is what I said...

75
00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.710
I mean, I absolutely thought
that it was completed then.

76
00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:53.710
But that Straw Hat guy,

77
00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:57.240
he's really a lot tougher
than you'd expect...

78
00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.800
So let me see if I understand...

79
00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:02.820
The report you gave
me was a complete lie?

80
00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.350
Well, yeah,
when you put it that way,

81
00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.500
I guess the report
wasn't the truth,

82
00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:10.180
But now, I've gotten rid
of that Straw Hat for sure,

83
00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:13.010
so there's no need for you
to send anyone else after him

84
00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.470
or the others...

85
00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:15.700
Very well...

86
00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.150
Take the pose and head straight

87
00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.310
to Alabasta from
there immediately.

88
00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.380
Do you understand me?

89
00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.480
But how are you still alive?

90
00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.350
The weapons...
They saved me...

91
00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:28.850
Weapons?

92
00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:30.550
Oh, yeah!
That makes sense!

93
00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.200
Not even weapons
that were made in Elbaph

94
00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.020
could hold up after
a hundred years

95
00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:35.460
of giants dueling
to the death with 'em!

96
00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.530
They must be dull by now!

97
00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.790
Now, that's a relief...

98
00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.170
It's a miracle, really!

99
00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:47.330
Brogy, would you let go...?

100
00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:49.130
I'm a little sore, here.

101
00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.400
I'm so glad you're
still alive, Dorry...

102
00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.230
It's amazing!
Gya, ba, ba, ba!

103
00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:57.570
Gya, gya, gya, gya!
Gya, gya, gya, gya!

104
00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:00.110
Come on, this wasn't a miracle.

105
00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:01.580
The fact that those
weapons are even intact

106
00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.230
after a century of fighting
is the miraculous part.

107
00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:05.600
They should be scrap by now.

108
00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:08.730
I'm surprised
they lasted this long.

109
00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:10.280
What a day this was...

110
00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.180
Thank you, God of Elbaph,
for this wonderful day!

111
00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:15.420
Oh, is that true, Brogy?

112
00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.190
You're saying that fighting
me while I was injured,

113
00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:20.660
cutting me down, and knocking
me out was all wonderful.

114
00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.250
Don't be an idiot, Dorry.

115
00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.580
That's not what I'm saying,
and you know it.

116
00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.400
Would you keep your
hands off my wounds?

117
00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:28.860
Gya, gya, gya, gya!

118
00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.200
Gya, ba, ba, ba!

119
00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.710
You try doing that
again and see how far you get!

120
00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:42.410
Yeah?! I could take
you down in a heartbeat!

121
00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:44.250
Yeah...!

122
00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:49.560
Duel...! Fight!

123
00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:52.430
You two are fighting
again, already?!

124
00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:53.810
We will have
no more radio contact

125
00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.960
from now on, understand?

126
00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.060
If Marines were to catch on
to what we're doing,

127
00:07:58.060 --> 00:07:59.700
that would be most unfortunate.

128
00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.370
From this point on, all of my
orders will be sent via letter,

129
00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:06.510
following the usual protocol.
That will be all, Mr. 3...

130
00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.420
Good luck on your mission.

131
00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.410
Miss All Sunday.

132
00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.170
Yes, sir?

133
00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:22.880
I want you to send Mr. 2

134
00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.890
to Little Garden immediately.

135
00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:25.990
Huh?

136
00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:29.400
Mr. 3 is on his way from
Little Garden to Alabasta.

137
00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.400
I want you to see
that he is eliminated...

138
00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.870
Perhaps that might be...
a little extreme, Crocodile.

139
00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:39.440
We still have plenty
of agents to spare.

140
00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.940
Are you arguing with me,
Miss All Sunday?

141
00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:43.340
No...

142
00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.540
I'll make the
arrangements at once.

143
00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.960
Consider it done.

144
00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.680
Well, he finally hung up...

145
00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.760
Now... I wonder
who these guys were...

146
00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.800
They sure are funny looking.

147
00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:03.860
What's this?

148
00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:09.700
<b>At Sea (The Grand Line)</b>

149
00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.610
Captain Smoker!

150
00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.700
I've just intercepted
a very intriguing signal!

151
00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.200
What is it?

152
00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.470
Ah!

153
00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.010
Such an incredible, full temper!

154
00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:18.880
The legendary... Kashu!

155
00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.670
Tashigi! Tashigi!

156
00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:22.830
Only here in the Grand Line

157
00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:26.790
could I find such a prized
sword as this so quickly!

158
00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:27.790
Tashigi!

159
00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.350
Come here!

160
00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:30.190
Are you deaf...?

161
00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:30.850
Ah!

162
00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:32.790
Yes, sir! Coming, Captain...

163
00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.190
Ah!

164
00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.930
Stop clowning
around and get over here!

165
00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.930
I need you to listen to this!

166
00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:44.790
Listen close...

167
00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.160
We just picked up this
conversation minutes ago...

168
00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:48.330
I've got it all queued up...

169
00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.590
Ready, Sergeant major?

170
00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:50.740
Uh... Yes...

171
00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.060
Play it back please...

172
00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:55.930
It's Mr. 0 now quit
fooling around, you jack ass...

173
00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:58.980
Have you eliminated Princess
Vivi and the Straw Hats...

174
00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:01.310
Straw hats? Straw Hat Pirates!

175
00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:02.010
Oh, yeah...

176
00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.150
The mission was successful...

177
00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:04.990
From this point on,

178
00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:07.360
all my orders will
be sent via letter

179
00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:10.130
<b>Black Wiretapper Snail</b>

180
00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:09.490
following the usual protocal...

181
00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:10.840
That will be all Mr. 3...

182
00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.540
And the rest of the message
is undecipherable static.

183
00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.030
It's a faint signal...

184
00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:17.360
But there are key
names and phrases

185
00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.860
laced in their conversation
that clearly stood out.

186
00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.060
Princess Vivi...

187
00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.400
Straw Hats...

188
00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.130
Orders via letter...

189
00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:27.070
And Mr. 0.

190
00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:30.280
Mr. 0? Could that be
a codename for somebody?!

191
00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.340
In fact, it's quite possible
he could be connected

192
00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.200
to that suspicious swordsman
we caught earlier in Runess.

193
00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:43.160
<b>Mr. 11
Frontier Agent, Baroque Works</b>

194
00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:38.360
What'd he say his
name was? Mr. 11?

195
00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.590
Possibly...

196
00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:43.250
Part of a criminal organization
that uses numbers for codenames

197
00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.040
and sends orders via letter...

198
00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.370
Sound about right?

199
00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.540
Ha! Mr. 0...? Organization...?

200
00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.920
I have no idea what
you're going on about.

201
00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:55.270
Then how do you explain
the letter of detailed orders

202
00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:56.990
we found in your pocket?

203
00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.730
Uh! Damn letter!

204
00:10:58.730 --> 00:10:59.830
I thought I burned it!

205
00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:02.930
Wait... That's not... not mine!

206
00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:04.430
That's funny...

207
00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:07.760
Because we didn't actually
find anything in your pocket.

208
00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.930
Ah!

209
00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.070
Hmm...

210
00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:15.930
All right, then...

211
00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.130
Princess Vivi...

212
00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.530
If I remember correctly,
she's from Alabasta

213
00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:21.500
and reports say
she's currently missing...

214
00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.370
Excuse me for interrupting,

215
00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.170
but isn't the Alabasta Kingdom
in the middle of a coup...?

216
00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:29.280
I wonder if this mysterious
criminal organization and the

217
00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.330
Straw Hat Pirates could somehow
be involved in the uprising?

218
00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:33.590
Who knows...

219
00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:36.330
All I know for certain is that
this is the only clue we have

220
00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:38.820
to the Straw Hat's whereabouts.

221
00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:39.550
This means...

222
00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:41.020
We're going...?

223
00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:41.850
Yes...

224
00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.540
I want you to
contact Headquarters

225
00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.560
and get an eternal pose!

226
00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.760
Yes, sir!

227
00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.530
It's time we pay
a little visit...

228
00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:53.990
...to Alabasta,
the kingdom of sand.

229
00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:58.070
<b>Little Garden, Island of Giants</b>

230
00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.750
We've been fighting so long
that we'd completely forgotten

231
00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.850
about the bounties
that were put on our heads.

232
00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.920
It has been a long time.

233
00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:13.690
But I'm the whole reason
that the Baroque Works agents

234
00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:15.420
came here in the first place...

235
00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.690
It's my fault.

236
00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:19.080
None of that anymore... Okay...?

237
00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:19.980
Yeah, come on, Vivi.

238
00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.580
Why are you so sad?

239
00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:23.680
Here, have a rice cracker.

240
00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.040
Uh, guys,
where did you get those?

241
00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.880
I know!
Let's have a rice cracker party!

242
00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.880
Rice crackers aren't
that exciting, though.

243
00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.980
Sure they are!
We can even toast with them.

244
00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.450
You see...?
Nobody's blaming you.

245
00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.020
Cheers!

246
00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:40.030
Hey, Luffy, don't do that!

247
00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.770
You can't just go
wasting food like that.

248
00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.810
Seriously,
you should know better.

249
00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:45.570
Hey, what are you doing?!

250
00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.610
Who said you could
have my cracker?

251
00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:48.410
Give it here!

252
00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.250
It's done! It's mine now!

253
00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.380
No, it's not!

254
00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:52.210
What's with you?

255
00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:54.170
Nothing... Just a bug bite.

256
00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:57.480
All right, I still can't believe
we have to wait here a year

257
00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:59.410
just for the log pose to reset.

258
00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:00.580
I know...

259
00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.750
It's definitely something
we should be worried about!

260
00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:04.920
All of you helped save us
from those other guys.

261
00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:08.840
If we can, we would really
like to return the favor.

262
00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:11.040
Well, maybe you guys could do
something about our log pose,

263
00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.710
so we won't be stuck here.

264
00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.110
Huh...

265
00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:16.430
I'm afraid the log pose
is the one thing

266
00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:17.780
that we can't help you with.

267
00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:18.850
Ahhh!

268
00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:23.280
Nami, dear! Vivi, my love!
And all the rest of you!

269
00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:25.950
Hey...! Sanji!

270
00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:30.000
You're all still okay...!
I'm so happy, so happy!

271
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.330
Of course, he's happy,
the big useless jerk...!

272
00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.800
He shows up after we've
taken care of everything!

273
00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.840
What the hell is going on?!

274
00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:41.530
Is one of you guys Mr. 3?

275
00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:44.910
Wait... and just how do you
know about Mr. 3 anyway?

276
00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:46.600
Nami...

277
00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:49.460
You look absolutely
amazing in that outfit!

278
00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.730
Say that again.

279
00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:52.030
Now, Nami...

280
00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:55.500
If you stand around dressed like
that all day, you'll catch cold.

281
00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:56.940
Here... Take my coat...

282
00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:58.510
Oh, thank you...

283
00:13:58.510 --> 00:13:59.810
So, I've been a little busy.

284
00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:00.710
I just finished talking

285
00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:04.490
to that Mr. 0 guy over
a transponder snail.

286
00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:05.990
Mr. 0?!

287
00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:06.990
Yeah, that guy...

288
00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.050
I was talking to him in
this weird hideout place

289
00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:10.800
I found in the jungle.

290
00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.930
He thought I was
some guy called Mr. 3,

291
00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.700
and I thought it would be a
good idea to let him believe it.

292
00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.040
And since I had him on the line,

293
00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:19.560
I went ahead and told him
that we were all dead.

294
00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.290
So he thinks he doesn't have to
send people after us anymore.

295
00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:24.170
So you're saying
that we're finally free

296
00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.480
of people chasing us now that
we can't go anywhere anyway?

297
00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:28.910
Oh... That is just perfect...

298
00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:30.080
We can't go? Why?

299
00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.910
Is there still something we
need to take care of here?

300
00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:34.550
That's a real shame
after I managed

301
00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:36.750
to get hold of this thing.

302
00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.070
Uh... what...?

303
00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.410
An eternal pose to
Alabasta...! All right!

304
00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:50.950
Now, we can set sail! Woo-hoo!

305
00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.520
Yes! Good job!

306
00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.620
I knew something would happen!

307
00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.020
Ohh...! Thank you!
Thank you so much!

308
00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:57.960
Thank you, Sanji!

309
00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.630
I was getting really
worried, thank you!

310
00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:03.470
No, no!
It was all my pleasure.

311
00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:05.630
I'm just glad I could
make you happy, Vivi.

312
00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:06.900
All right, everyone!

313
00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.200
Now we're having
a rice cracker party!

314
00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.090
No way. Look, Luffy,

315
00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:13.380
we don't have
enough left for a party.

316
00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:14.550
There's only three.

317
00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:15.780
What?!

318
00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:16.550
It doesn't matter.

319
00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:18.520
We don't have time
for that anyway.

320
00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:19.390
Come on now, Captain.

321
00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.990
We don't have time
to be sitting here.

322
00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.060
Zoro! Hold on a sec.

323
00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:29.590
So, uh, you forget
about our hunting contest?

324
00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:32.230
Nope. Hate to
tell you this, but you lost.

325
00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:34.590
I caught a rhino
that was this big.

326
00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:38.060
That doesn't sound very tasty,
but I guess you can eat it.

327
00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:39.990
Sounds just fine to me.

328
00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:43.450
Hunting contest?

329
00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:46.450
Something about that
sounds familiar somehow.

330
00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:48.490
Hmm...

331
00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:51.160
'Kay... Giant old guys,

332
00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:53.920
it's really been
a lot of fun, but we gotta go.

333
00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:54.850
Hm?

334
00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:55.790
Hmm?

335
00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:57.560
Of course... Right...

336
00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.130
We can tell you
need to get going.

337
00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:01.800
It's too bad that you
have to leave so soon.

338
00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:03.760
I hope you get to
your homeland in time.

339
00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.530
Me too. Thank you.

340
00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:09.020
See ya...!
Try not to die anymore, okay?

341
00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:10.120
Quaaaack!

342
00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:10.950
Master...

343
00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:13.140
I'm going to go
visit Elbaph someday!

344
00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:14.600
You just wait and see.

345
00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:16.620
My catch is much
bigger than yours.

346
00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.320
Hmph! You wish.

347
00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.000
I'm gonna be
a brave warrior of the sea!

348
00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:27.510
Our friends are setting sail.

349
00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:30.390
That's right, and
we can't just sit here,

350
00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:32.510
not when there's a monster
waiting for them in the sea.

351
00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.930
So, Dorry,
how are your wounds doing?

352
00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:40.450
These...? I think
I can live with them.

353
00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:46.660
It's safe to say that our
weapons are about worn through.

354
00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.200
Any regrets?

355
00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:51.370
It's difficult to give up...

356
00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:54.710
I've fought with this axe for
more than a hundred years,

357
00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.710
but if it's a sacrifice for our
friends, then it's worth it.

358
00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.850
Yeah, I agree...

359
00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:12.630
See, I told you mine
was bigger than yours.

360
00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:13.700
I win!

361
00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.810
You should look closer!
My lizard is much bigger!

362
00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:17.920
What, are you
blind or something...?

363
00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.550
My rhino is obviously
so much larger

364
00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:20.730
than your stupid lizard is.

365
00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:22.030
It doesn't really matter...

366
00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:24.290
They both look yummy.

367
00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.910
– Just shut up, Luffy!
– Just shut up, Luffy!

368
00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:27.050
Yours doesn't even have horns...

369
00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:28.680
What does that
have to do with anything...?

370
00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.250
Size! Yours is puny...

371
00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:33.540
Children, how long
are you going to fight...?

372
00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.810
We don't need all of it, anyway,

373
00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:37.940
just cut up what we do need, so
we can get out of here, already.

374
00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:40.220
Right...! Of course, Nami!

375
00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.770
Hey, Usopp! Would you tell him
that I'm clearly the winner?

376
00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:45.270
No, I really don't care.

377
00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:47.210
Can't you just agree it's a tie?

378
00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.310
I don't believe in ties.

379
00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:49.280
I fight to win.

380
00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.980
Just hurry up, you two!

381
00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:53.980
Yeah!

382
00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:00.430
Set sail!

383
00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:06.800
The giants said that
going straight would take us

384
00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:08.540
to the western end
of the island...

385
00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.730
Hey! Couldn't you guys

386
00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:11.160
have gotten any
more meat on board?

387
00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:12.330
Yeah, right.

388
00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.760
We can't possibly
preserve any more than this.

389
00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.930
It would just spoil
before we could eat it

390
00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:20.500
Are you actively
trying to sink the ship?

391
00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:24.120
Hey! Look at that;
it's the giants!

392
00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.720
They must have come
down here to say goodbye.

393
00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:32.880
A great danger
still lies ahead of you.

394
00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.640
It is an obstacle that
has always been here.

395
00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:39.140
Trying to prevent people from
reaching the next island.

396
00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.780
Uhh...

397
00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:42.900
Everyone of you
fought like true warriors

398
00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:45.130
in order to protect
the pride of our duel...

399
00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.730
And because you
were willing to do that,

400
00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.900
no matter what
enemy you may face...

401
00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.070
We will never let them
destroy your pride, friends.

402
00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:59.700
You must have faith in
what we say. Go straight...

403
00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.880
No matter what happens,
keep going straight.

404
00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:03.820
Understand?

405
00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:06.060
Yeah, got it...

406
00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:07.710
What was that about?

407
00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:09.830
I don't get it.
What'd he say?

408
00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:13.000
No matter what happens,
we just go straight!

409
00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.840
This is goodbye.

410
00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.440
Let's meet again someday.

411
00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:24.670
Absolutely.

412
00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:25.730
Look! Over there!

413
00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.370
Hello, Island-Eater.

414
00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:35.870
You will open the path...

415
00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:38.400
In the name of Elbaph,
you will open it!

416
00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.700
Quaaack!

417
00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.890
It's a monster!

418
00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.270
What the heck is
that guy? A goldfish?

419
00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:13.510
It's a... giant goldfish?

420
00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:14.510
Usopp, hey!

421
00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:16.350
Start working the rudder
or we're gonna be eaten!

422
00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:17.280
Hurry it up!

423
00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:20.880
Yeah... I know but,
we have to go straight ahead...

424
00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.420
Isn't that right, Luffy?

425
00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:23.520
Mm-hmm.

426
00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:25.050
We sure do.

427
00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:31.900
Don't be a moron, Luffy!

428
00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:35.030
This isn't going to be anything
like what happened with Laboon.

429
00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:36.100
Yeah, I know...

430
00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:37.600
Now, calm down...

431
00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.720
Here... I'll let you
have the last rice cracker.

432
00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:41.210
I don't want a cracker!

433
00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.890
If we don't turn the
ship around right now,

434
00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:44.410
that thing is gonna eat us.

435
00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:45.910
Quaaack!

436
00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:47.140
Nami, just give it up.

437
00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:53.000
Luffy! You really sure

438
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.450
we can trust
those little pals of yours?

439
00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:56.250
Yup!

440
00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:57.130
Are we actually
going to willingly

441
00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.700
head straight into
that beast's belly?!

442
00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:03.840
Uh-huh! It's too
late to turn now!

443
00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:14.720
You've sure gotten a
lot bigger, Island-Eater...

444
00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:16.290
Filthy goldfish.

445
00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:17.260
And his size isn't

446
00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:19.930
the only surprising
thing about him, either.

447
00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:21.780
There's also the dung
that he produces

448
00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:23.800
after he devours a island.

449
00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.330
The size of that stuff
is quite impressive...

450
00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:29.660
I recall one specimen that's
known as Nothing At All Island.

451
00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.990
Yes... We landed
on it a long time ago

452
00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:37.100
and thought it was real
land we were standing on.

453
00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.770
I'm beginning
to feel nostalgic...

454
00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:39.950
Watching them sail in,

455
00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:42.540
I remember my old
adventurous days.

456
00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:49.610
The only thing that we
can't pierce with this weapon,

457
00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:51.880
is the great bloodstained snake.

458
00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:52.820
Together our weapons

459
00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:55.450
form the most powerful
weapon Elbaph can offer.

460
00:21:55.450 --> 00:21:57.320
The giant spear...

461
00:22:00.850 --> 00:22:03.090
Just go straight...!
Go straight!

462
00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:06.810
What does it matter...?!
We've already been eaten here!

463
00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.730
Straight, okay?!
Just keep going!

464
00:22:17.570 --> 00:22:19.610
– Hakoku!
– Hakoku!

465
00:22:24.270 --> 00:22:26.600
We're flying!

466
00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:33.460
Hmph.

467
00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:34.720
Don't bother lookin back!

468
00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:37.630
'Cause we're goin' straight ahead!

469
00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:44.470
Look at us! This is so incredible!

470
00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:48.350
They cut... the sea... itself!

471
00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:54.440
The strength of... the Elbaph
Warriors... is amazing!

472
00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:10.360
Friends!

473
00:23:14.640 --> 00:23:17.540
Go... Good luck!

474
00:23:26.370 --> 00:23:27.970
Long ago, the sea
was ruled by colossal,

475
00:23:28.990 --> 00:23:32.730
swashbuckling ruffians known
as the Giant Warrior Pirates...

476
00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:35.080
Living only for the thrill
of battle and conquest,

477
00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:37.920
these pirates laid waste
to all who opposed them.

478
00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:42.490
They were presided over by two bosses,
Red Ogre Brogy and Blue Ogre Dorry,

479
00:23:42.490 --> 00:23:44.360
both exceptionally strong...

480
00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:47.000
The power and influence they
held went largely unchecked,

481
00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:48.860
for no other giant was their equal

482
00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:51.530
and ordinary men cowered
in their massive shadows.

483
00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:53.970
This made the fact that a lone
little girl single-handedly

484
00:23:53.970 --> 00:23:57.110
put an end to their attacks
all the more surprising.

485
00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:01.770
Our two bosses are truly great!

486
00:24:01.770 --> 00:24:03.200
Did you hear about their catch?!

487
00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:04.100
Yeah!

488
00:24:04.100 --> 00:24:05.940
I can hardly think about anything else!

489
00:24:05.940 --> 00:24:07.640
It's so exciting!

490
00:24:07.640 --> 00:24:11.140
It's not every day someone
bags a huge sea king!

491
00:24:11.140 --> 00:24:12.640
And they each got one...

492
00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:13.910
Now, that's impressive...

493
00:24:13.910 --> 00:24:16.720
Yeah. Take us for example,
we're Elbaph giants.

494
00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:19.720
No greater warrior exists,
but even we don't come close

495
00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:22.190
to taking down one of
those massive beasts...

496
00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.090
Wouldn't you say that's fair, men?!

497
00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:25.490
Yeah!

498
00:24:25.850 --> 00:24:26.950
Our bosses are the best!

499
00:24:29.490 --> 00:24:33.620
I bet... that no one's ever
slain a bigger sea king than us!

500
00:24:36.060 --> 00:24:38.560
A conquest destined to become legend!

501
00:24:41.630 --> 00:24:43.800
Awesome! So which one was bigger?!

502
00:24:43.860 --> 00:24:44.690
Hm?

503
00:24:44.690 --> 00:24:45.560
What?

504
00:24:46.830 --> 00:24:47.860
Which one?

505
00:24:47.860 --> 00:24:48.700
Mm-hm!

506
00:24:49.180 --> 00:24:51.220
Who won the contest, you or Brogy?

507
00:24:52.320 --> 00:24:54.250
– Hmm...
– Hmm...

508
00:24:56.090 --> 00:24:57.980
Look at them side-by-side, Brogy!

509
00:24:57.980 --> 00:24:59.480
Mine is slightly bigger, see?!

510
00:24:59.480 --> 00:25:00.420
Keep dreaming!

511
00:25:00.420 --> 00:25:03.250
Mine beats yours by
three whole centimeters!

512
00:25:03.250 --> 00:25:04.890
What?! You're joking!

513
00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:05.820
No!

514
00:25:05.820 --> 00:25:09.090
Bosses, please! Stop bickering!

515
00:25:15.990 --> 00:25:17.940
I suppose I should mention Brogy...

516
00:25:17.940 --> 00:25:22.210
I recall something about a hunting contest,
but I can't exactly remember...

517
00:25:22.210 --> 00:25:23.180
Don't worry, Dorry.

518
00:25:23.180 --> 00:25:25.410
The same thing goes for me.

519
00:25:27.460 --> 00:25:28.460
– Hmm?
– Hmm?

520
00:25:28.460 --> 00:25:30.430
It's Middle Mountain!

521
00:25:30.430 --> 00:25:31.600
So...

522
00:25:31.600 --> 00:25:34.430
What do ya say... you and
I go ahead and finish this?!

523
00:25:34.430 --> 00:25:35.470
Sure...!

524
00:25:35.470 --> 00:25:38.440
We can always think
things through after that!

525
00:25:48.630 --> 00:25:52.200
The scope of this planet's so vast and so grand

526
00:25:52.160 --> 00:25:55.550
That if treasure's out there, well where do you start?

527
00:25:55.500 --> 00:25:58.840
Keep your wits about you, don’t leave it to chance

528
00:25:58.860 --> 00:26:02.940
Yeah play it smart but don’t forget
that in the end you’re still rolling the dice

529
00:26:04.980 --> 00:26:06.110
And that's why...

530
00:26:08.850 --> 00:26:12.140
If someone gets in our way, well who cares?

531
00:26:12.190 --> 00:26:15.530
If someone’s running their mouth, well who cares?

532
00:26:15.510 --> 00:26:21.020
Let's sail out, yeah we'll tell all the losers here "bon voyage"

533
00:26:20.780 --> 00:26:22.710
Get lost and stay

534
00:26:22.470 --> 00:26:28.830
Cause even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna get it done

535
00:26:28.840 --> 00:26:35.410
The more impossible the impressive, reach for the stars

536
00:26:35.520 --> 00:26:42.130
Yeah, even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna take you on

537
00:26:42.160 --> 00:26:48.800
If we can sail across this vast sea we’ll find a paradise

538
00:26:49.150 --> 00:26:54.510
Go ahead and give it your best,
next time you look out your telescope

539
00:26:54.270 --> 00:26:56.310
You’ll find you’re one step closer
